# Verify on the live site

Browser and compendium checks use the live app at
`https://alter-ego.apps.masche.at`. This workspace has no full compendium
database, and a local app server does not stay up. `npm start`, `npm run dev`,
`dev:all`, `dev:src`, and Vite are not a valid check.

Node scripts and static checks that do not serve the app stay allowed
(`npm test`, one-off scripts, `npm run build:app`).

## When a change needs the live database or a browser pass

1. Commit the relevant files. Leave out secrets and scratch files such as
   `tmp-verify-*.mjs`.
2. Merge that branch into `main` and push `main`. This standing instruction is
   the explicit go-ahead for that verification deploy. If the merge is not
   clean, stop and report it. Never force-push.
3. Stop. Tell the user that `main` is pushed and that they deploy Alter Ego
   by hand from the Server Management project. Do not open
   `D:\Projects\ServerManagement`. Do not switch the Cursor workspace. A
   workspace switch aborts the handoff. Pushing does not deploy by itself.
   Coolify builds `main` only when that app is deployed.
4. After the user says that deploy is healthy, stay in this project and
   exercise the changed flow on `https://alter-ego.apps.masche.at`.
   `/api/health` should report `"compendium":"sqlite"`.
